# Measurement pipeline rules

- Do keep dedupe logic in `02_count_tokens.py` (analysis), not in the crawler,
  because silently dropping catalogs at collection time hides evidence.
- Do preserve the `count_method` column and its estimate/tiktoken distinction;
  rows marked `estimate:*` must never feed a headline statistic, because only
  tokenizer-true counts are quotable on stage.
- Do treat `collect_log.csv` as append-only attempt history, because the
  retry trail (fail at 10:02, succeed at 11:40) is audit evidence, not noise.
- Do keep one serialization recipe (compact JSON, sorted keys, unicode kept)
  for every server, because formatting drift would masquerade as design drift.
- Do not change data-dictionary field definitions without flagging it as a
  methods-note change, because frozen definitions are what make N comparable
  across crawl extensions.
- When adding any new derived statistic, print the code path that produced it
  in BUILDLOG.md, because every number needs a reproducible origin.
